      "message": "The purpose to introduce new flag, GPIO_PSL_ACTHIGH, is that we don’t know the active polarity of GPIO input from gpio.inc if the board uses PSL for hibernate functionality. \n\nFor example, LID_OPEN is one of hibernate inputs and we used to declare it as below in gpio.inc.\nGPIO_INT(LID_OPEN, PIN(A, 6), GPIO_INT_BOTH | GPIO_PULL_DOWN, lid_interrupt)\nIf the board uses PSL mode for hibernating, we need external PU/PD for PSL inputs and internal weak PU/PD are unnecessary since they will influence the impedance of external PU/PD. And we might declare it as:\nGPIO_INT(LID_OPEN, PIN(0, 1), GPIO_INT_BOTH, lid_interrupt)\n\nIn order to determine the active polarity of PSL input, adding a new GPIO_PSL_ACTHIGH flag for PSL inputs might look below:\nGPIO_INT(AC_PRESENT, PIN(D, 2), GPIO_INT_BOTH, extpower_interrupt) -\u003e high to low (falling edge) or low-level trigger.\nGPIO_INT(POWER_BUTTON_L, PIN(0, 0), GPIO_INT_BOTH, power_button_interrupt) -\u003e (falling edge) high to low or low-level trigger.\nGPIO_INT(LID_OPEN, PIN(0, 1), GPIO_INT_BOTH | GPIO_PSL_ACTHIGH, lid_interrupt) -\u003e (rasing edge) low to high or high-level trigger.\n\nAny suggestion is highly appreciated.",
